src('SRC048','UFOs at Missile Base: AARO Deputy Director Misstates Facts (blog repost of Hastings email to AARO members, 4-6 Aug 2025, quoting Marik von Rennenkampff)','Robert Hastings / Marik von Rennenkampff (reposted by Occult Mystic)','occultmystic.blogspot.com','2025-08-07','Advocacy blog repost of an email','SECONDARY','https://occultmystic.blogspot.com/2025/08/ufos-at-missile-base-aaro-deputy.html','','intro and Malmstrom section','%s'%A,'INC019;EVD089','Reports AARO ex-deputy director Phillips said a cascading transformer failure from an electrical storm caused Echo; says a 6 Jun 2025 WSJ story citing AARO officials said an unannounced EMP test did; quotes 341st SMW histories (Jan-Mar 1967: commercial power switching not the cause; later histories: power tests essentially negative, EMP speculated).','Advocacy; second-hand paraphrase of AARO statements; the AARO report and WSJ story not seen by me.','INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE','EXAMINED')
ev('EVD089',"AARO's explanation for Echo, as far as I can establish: only second-hand. Per an advocate email (SRC048), ex-AARO deputy director Phillips said in interviews that a 'cascading transformer failure' triggered by an 'electrical storm' caused the shutdown, while a 6 Jun 2025 WSJ story citing AARO officials reportedly said an unannounced EMP test did; neither is in a primary AARO document that I could open (the Volume I historical report PDF could not be downloaded: 403/empty responses from aaro.mil, media.defense.gov and fas.org). Comparison with the wing history (SRC002): a 7.2 kV transformer did short near Winifred at ~1450 on 16 March, 6 hours after the 0845 shutdown, and the history ruled out weather and power switching as the cause, so a 'transformer cascade' explanation does not fit the timing or the record as transcribed; the same history says no cause was found. Hastings's email says later wing histories (mid-1967 and about a year later) record power tests as 'essentially negative' and speculate an EMP cause; I did not see those histories. An EMP-test explanation is therefore unsupported by any document I have, and the AARO transformer explanation conflicts with the one I have. AARO's actual wording is unknown to me.",'ANALYST_ASSESSMENT','SRC048; SRC002; search results','INC019;EVD085;EVD088;RQ025','10099','HIGH','INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE')
